From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:37:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: psci: export psci_cpu_suspend_enter

The MT6797 SPM module enters SODI with CPU0 powered down through the
firmware, as the vendor does: it loads and starts the SPM program, then
issues CPU_SUSPEND for the cluster and resumes at cpu_resume when the
program powers the core back on. Export the helper that does the PSCI
call with the context save, so a module can use it.
---
 drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
index e73bae6cb..52e2567e5 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
@@ -525,6 +525,7 @@ int psci_cpu_suspend_enter(u32 state)
 
 	return ret;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(psci_cpu_suspend_enter);
 #endif
 
 static int psci_system_suspend(unsigned long unused)
-- 
2.43.0

